  "title": "Marshall Islands stick charts",
  "summary": "Marshallese navigators made wooden stick charts to teach apprentices how ocean swells behave around islands. The meddo type shows swells and the islands of the chain; the mattang type is a simpler diagram of swells meeting islands. Museums record such charts from the 19th century onward.",
